    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (80.77) and **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) are our unequivocal anchors. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** draws a highly favorable matchup against Klassen, whose 5.56 xERA provides the perfect runway for our star third baseman to capitalize on his 3-hole positioning. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from the 10% park factor boost at Matthews\u2019 home field, combined with a dynamic platoon edge that vaults his efficiency well into the \"Strong\" start tier. We are also leaning heavily into the speed-utility profile of **Zack Gelof** (62.22), whose ability to exploit Matthews' slow delivery should be a boon for our scarce SB category today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Gavin Sheets** (40.24) out of the lineup. While he offers solid power, his efficiency is capped by Ashcraft\u2019s 3.28 xERA and a poor park factor, ultimately losing his spot to the higher upside of **Justin Crawford** and **JJ Bleday**. The latter is a high-conviction start today, boasting a 65.58 score due to an excellent platoon edge against the lefty Whisenhunt, despite his bottom-of-the-order ranking. Conversely, we must exercise caution with **Cal Raleigh** (41.14) and **Justin Crawford** (43.20); both face the significant hurdle of Wheeler and Gilbert, respectively. **Cal Raleigh** is battling a formidable SP skill disadvantage, and **Justin Crawford** is heavily penalized by his #9 spot in the order, keeping them near the lower bound of our start threshold. We are monitoring the lineup status for **Jung Hoo Lee**, as any shift from the projected #6 spot could necessitate a mid-day pivot.",
